{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"7b984bfc-ff1b-43ec-8947-a9b602c77ce2","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have added the `codex-sandboxed` lane to [run.sh](file:///tmp/h-WAolLd/run.sh) and documented the changes and colleague note applicability in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-WAolLd/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Changes:\n1. **Added `codex-sandboxed` Lane in [run.sh](file:///tmp/h-WAolLd/run.sh)**:\n   - Added `codex-sandboxed` to the usage comment and `case` dispatcher.\n   - Implemented `codex_sandboxed_run()` matching the sandbox configuration in `kimi_run()`:\n     - Uses `sandbox-exec -D HOME=\"$REAL\" -f \"$D/sandbox/agent.sb\"`.\n     - Assigns a fresh temporary scratch directory in `/tmp` as `$HOME` (`export HOME=\"$SH\"`).\n     - Passes `-o \"$SC/final.txt\"` targeting a temporary scratch folder in `/tmp`, copying the resulting `final.txt` into `$R/final.txt` once `sandbox-exec` returns (resolving the issue where writing to `$R` inside the user's home folder is denied by `agent.sb`).\n     - Cleans up scratch directories and preserves the command exit code.\n2. **Updated Documentation**:\n   - Updated [README.md](file:///tmp/h-WAolLd/README.md) to document the `codex-sandboxed` lane.\n   - Wrote [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-WAolLd/ANSWER.md) detailing the changes and specifying which parts of the colleague's note applied and which were ignored.\n","duration_seconds":114.023475,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":220952,"output_tokens":4237,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":341872,"total_tokens":225189}}}
